<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Empire of Japan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Imperial Japan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Empire of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> was the Japanese state from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/meiji-restoration">Meiji Restoration</a> of 1868 until the post-war <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-japan">constitution of 1947</a>. It modernised rapidly, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, acquired colonies including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taiwan">Taiwan</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, and expanded across East and South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> before its defeat in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a> in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/empire-of-japan.jpg" alt="Empire of Japan" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: kahusi - (Talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Japan_(1870%E2%80%931999).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
